course: dictionary
lesson: 4998
title: Meet the indri
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An indri is a kind of lemur, and a lemur is an animal that lives mostly in trees. Good readers use the words around a new word to find its meaning. «The indri is the biggest living lemur and sings loud songs in family groups.» The sentence tells you the indri is big, lives with its family, and sings.
explain: Look for more clues. «Lemurs are primates, cousins of monkeys and apes.» The word cousins tells you lemurs are related to monkeys and apes, even though they are not the same animal. The dictionary adds that indris are black and white and live only in the rainforests of Madagascar.
explain: Always check your meaning. Put it in the sentence in place of the hard word. If an indri is a big, black-and-white tree animal that sings, does «the indri's song» make sense? Yes, so you have understood it.
fact: An indri is the largest kind of lemur.
fact: Lemurs are primates, cousins of monkeys and apes.
fact: Indris live only in the rainforests of Madagascar, an island.
fact: Indris live in family groups, eat leaves and leap between trees.
fact: Indris are critically endangered because their forest is being cut down.
exercise: «The indri is the biggest living lemur.» What is an indri? | A bird that lives in the desert | *A kind of lemur, the largest one | A sort of fish from the sea | A tiny insect that lives in gardens
exercise: Where do indris live in the wild? | In the deserts of Africa | *In the rainforests of Madagascar | On farms in Scotland | In the mountains of Antarctica
exercise: Why are indris in danger? | They are too small to find food | They have stopped singing | *Their forest is being cut down | They live in cities
test: In «Lemurs are primates, cousins of monkeys and apes», what does cousins suggest? | Animals that cannot climb | *Animals closely related to monkeys and apes | Animals that eat only bananas | Animals that live in the same tree
test: «Scientists found rhythms in indri songs, a little like music.» What does a little like music suggest? | The songs are only heard at night | The songs are as loud as thunder | The songs are sad and quiet | *The songs have a pattern, a bit like a tune
exam: Nadia reads «the indri's song» and thinks an indri is a bird. Which clue shows she is wrong? | Indris are found in London parks | An indri is a sort of blue flower | The word song is always about birds | *The sentences say the indri is the biggest lemur, a tree-living animal
